Error [jet.PersistentMutableBorrow]: A mutable borrow of `count` cannot escape its persistent or static storage cell
  --> tests/ui/e0223_static_cell_mutable_borrow.jet:9:11
    |
  9 |     bump(&count)
    |           ^^^^^
 Why: Persistent and static state must be changed by computing a replacement and assigning the whole binding. A mutable borrow or mutating receiver would let access escape the cell.
 Fix: Compute an owned replacement, then assign the persistent or static binding as a whole instead of passing `count` with `&` or using a mutating receiver.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0223
